{"role":"system","content":"## Available Skills\n\nThis list reflects what's available right now, in this turn — skills can be added or removed while a session is running. If it disagrees with something you or the user said about skill availability earlier in this conversation, this current list is the accurate one.\n\n- **batch**: Plan a sweeping mechanical change (rename, refactor, migration) and run it in parallel worktree-isolated agents. When the change is mechanical, decomposable, and affects many files.\n- **debug**: Diagnose a bug or failing test by gathering evidence before forming a hypothesis. When something is broken or behaving unexpectedly.\n- **import**: Detect and import configuration from Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor into this project's AGENTS.md/.agents/.atta layout. When the user asks to import/migrate settings from Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor, or runs /import.\n- **init**: Guide the user through initializing a new AGENTS.md file for a project. When starting a new project that lacks documentation, or when the user asks to create an AGENTS.md.\n- **keybindings-help**: Show keyboard shortcuts and key bindings reference for the CLI/TUI. When the user asks about keyboard shortcuts, key bindings, or how to navigate the CLI/TUI.\n- **loop**: Run a prompt or task on a recurring interval (poll status / monitor process). When the user asks to keep running something every N minutes, watch a build, etc.\n- **loremIpsum**: Generate placeholder text of a requested length / structure for prototypes. When prototyping UI / docs and any placeholder text will do.\n- **remember**: Save a fact / preference / decision to cross-session memory (~/.atta/memory). When the user explicitly asks to remember something, or you learn a stable preference.\n- **rename**: Rename the current conversation session with a descriptive title. When the user says 'rename this session' or 'give this conversation a title'.\n- **security-review**: Review pending code changes for security vulnerabilities and report findings. Before opening a PR or merging; when handling secrets, auth, crypto, or user-supplied data.\n- **simplify**: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency; then fix what's found. After making non-trivial changes; before opening a PR.\n- **skillify**: Turn a recently-executed workflow into a reusable SKILL.md. After a multi-step task that the user might run again — capture the playbook.\n- **stuck**: When you're not making progress: stop, write down what you know, what you've tried, what you'd try next, and ask the user for direction. After 3+ failed attempts at the same goal; when going in circles.\n- **updateConfig**: Make a precise edit to settings.json (permissions / hooks / mcp_servers) with backup. When the user wants to add a permission rule, register a hook, or wire an MCP server.\n- **verify**: Verify a change does what it should by running the app and exercising the new path. After implementing a feature/fix; before reporting it as done.\n","name":"skills.catalog"}